---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { EMBED_PATH, embedSnippet, embedSri } from '../lib/embed-sri.js';
---

<Base title="Embed a take-home estimate: Takehome" engine={false}>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Embed</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      One script tag. The salary is calculated in the reader’s browser with
      the same T4127 engine as the rest of Takehome. No cookie. No pixel. No
      salary posted back to us. Pin this path: it is immutable: and keep
      the SRI hash so a CDN swap cannot silently change the widget.
    </p>

    <pre><code>{embedSnippet()}</code></pre>
    <p>
      Subresource Integrity: <code>{embedSri()}</code>. Hosts must send{' '}
      <code>crossorigin="anonymous"</code> with the hash.
    </p>

    <p>
      Job boards, recruiters, and relocation services: put that on a listing
      and the candidate sees take-home on the posted salary before they open
      another tab. You get a calculator your readers keep; we get a link to
      the formulas. The same engine publishes every disagreement with the
      CRA’s own calculator, including all 164 one-cent cases, and the 1
      January 2027 CPP rate change you will have to implement.
    </p>

    <h2>Live on this page</h2>
    <p>Ontario, $75,000 a year, claim code 1, July 2026 rules:</p>
    <script
      is:inline
      src={EMBED_PATH}
      integrity={embedSri()}
      crossorigin="anonymous"
      data-province="ON"
      data-gross="75000"></script>
  </article>
</Base>
